Figure 1. (Left) CLIP’s anomaly unawareness: Category-level image-text alignment in pre-training leads to CLIP’s vague distinctions
in anomaly/normal semantics and inaccurate patch-text alignment. (Middle) Our two-stage adaptation strategy: In Stage1, anomaly
and normal text features are disentangled as anchors in text space; in Stage2, patch-level visual features are trained to align to these an-
chors, forming Anomaly-Aware CLIP. (Right) Generalizable anomaly awareness: Our method enables CLIP with generalizable anomaly
awareness for both known and unseen classes.

