Figure 4. The Two-Stage Training Pipeline of Anomaly-Aware CLIP. In the first stage, the text encoder of AA-CLIP is trained to
identify anomaly-related semantics, helped by a disentangle loss. In the second stage, patch features are aligned with these text anchors.
Both stages are achieved by the integration of Residual Adapters into the shallow layers of CLIP’s backbone. This controlled adaptation
enables CLIP to effectively distinguish anomalies, which forms our Anomaly-Aware CLIP.

